    <!-- ABOUT -->
    <section class="section" id="about">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">INTRODUCTION</p>
        <h2>About Me</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-content">
        <p>
          I am a PhD Research Scholar in the Department of Mathematics
          at the Indian Institute of Technology Ropar, India, working
          under the supervision of
          <a href="https://manmohanvashisth.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Dr. Manmohan Vashisth
          </a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          My research interests lie in inverse problems for partial
          differential equations, particularly in the uniqueness,
          reconstruction, and stability of time-dependent coefficients.
          I am interested in analytical techniques such as Carleman
          estimates, complex geometrical optics solutions, and
          microlocal analysis.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- RESEARCH -->
    <section class="section section-alt" id="research">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">ACADEMIC INTERESTS</p>
        <h2>Research Interests</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="research-grid">
        <article class="research-card">
          <h3>Inverse Problems</h3>
          <p>
            Uniqueness, reconstruction, and stability in inverse
            boundary value problems for partial differential equations.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="research-card">
          <h3>Partial Differential Equations</h3>
          <p>
            Schrödinger, heat, wave, and Klein–Gordon equations,
            including their coupled and nonlinear forms.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="research-card">
          <h3>Analytical Methods</h3>
          <p>
            Carleman estimates, complex geometrical optics solutions,
            geometric optics solutions, and microlocal analysis.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="research-card">
          <h3>Coefficient Identification</h3>
          <p>
            Determination of time-dependent potentials, convection
            coefficients, and nonlinear terms from boundary measurements.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

